    --------------------------------------------------------------------
    So what DOES make Mission Impossible such a great board? Well, for
    one thing, it's the sheer size of the board. Four nodes online, 3.1
    GIGABYTES of disk space and growing all the time....

    Where many boards have 1000 or so files to download,  Mission
    Impossible currently has around 24,000 - with 1000 new ones being
    added every *month*.  Imagine: 25 to 30 new files every DAY! Our
    target is 45,000 files and we have the space and the resource to
    meet that target.

    Where many boards have 300 or so users,  Mission Impossible has
    well over 3700 at the time of writing - and around 250 new users
    join every month.  Many of them are computer professionals who are
    willing and able to answer your software and hardware queries.

    Where many boards have a few new messages each time you call,
    Mission Impossible has 8000 new messages every *4 weeks*. Many are
    serious, many are frivolous, but all are entertaining.
    
    Where many boards have just one line, Mission Impossible has four -
    2 feature Courier HST modems, 1 features the 14,400 bps Courier Dual
    Standard and 1 features a Compucom 9600 bps Speedmodem. Four high
    speed lines to connect you to Mission Impossible!

    If you're looking for a particular file,  chances are the board
    will have it.  If not, new files are downloaded from the USA every
    week and Subscribers are able to make requests for special files
    that they would like "importing" from the USA.

    If you're an old-hand at comms or if you're just getting started,
    Mission Impossible is the board for you.  The software used is
    Wildcat: renowned for its simplicity of use as well as its power
    and flexibility. And everyone is warmly welcomed, whether they
    call dozens of boards each week or whether Mission Impossible is
    the very first board they have ever called!

    Remember, three nodes of Mission Impossible are entirely free!
    They offer uses access to almost all of the facilites that we
    provide and there are no fees for access to nodes 2,3 and 4 at all.

    Mission Impossible is so popular that it can be hard to connect -
    especially during peak times.  But subscribers get their own
    uncrowded node - and the promise of further subscriber-only nodes
    if the first one gets too busy.  Subscribers also enjoy NO file
    ratios: there is absolutely no need to upload in order to download
    (although uploads earn yet more benefits and privileges).  And
    subscribers get one hour of online time a day, 1 megabyte of
    downloads a day and, of course, access to those "hot" files direct
    from the States.

    Membership is just œ25 for a full year.  50p a week or
    thereabouts.  For access to so much hardware and software
    assistance and for access to so many Public Domain and Shareware
    files, we think it's a bargain.

    To join, simply send your cheque, postal order or even cash, to
    Keith Barnes, Mission Impossible BBS at the address below.

